Title: Judge's X Word Puzzle No. 31
Author: Harold O. Keedy
Date: 1927-12-24
Byline: Submitted by Harold O. Keedy, Martinsburg, W. Va. Judge pays $10 for each puzzle printed.
Date-Note: fix file; archive.org metadata says 1927-12-17
Source: https://archive.org/details/sim_judge_1927-12-17_93/page/n31/mode/1up
Puzzle-Number: 31
Solution-Source: https://archive.org/details/sim_judge_1927-12-31_93/page/n31/mode/1up


CHRISTMAS#GIFTS
LOAN#OASIS#SOOT
IMP#F#NIGHT#GOO
ME#MAD#AHEAP#KC
B#NAKED#TAPER#K
#BASINET#RET#SI
MOTOR#MOLES#PAN
IRAN#CUPID#HANG
SOL#PERIL#SORTS
TN#WAN#CANTATA#
L#WAIST#CARRY#H
EH#SNOWS#BUD#PO
TAP#TRILL#T#SAL
ORAL#SNAIL#HELL
EPSOM#SPEAKEASY


A1. On what day does Daddy get it in the neck? ~ CHRISTMAS
A9. What comes from the 5 and 10? ~ GIFTS
A14. What does the family want from the kin they love to touch? ~ LOAN
A15. What does the average cellar resemble during the holidays? ~ OASIS
A17. What comes down the chimney on Christmas? ~ SOOT
A18. What does no boy choose to be just before Christmas? ~ IMP
A20. When does Santa do most of his work? ~ NIGHT
A22. What do you call the dressing on plum pudding? ~ GOO
A23. Name an egotistical pronoun. ~ ME
A24. What kind of people are crazy about Christmas? ~ MAD
A26. How does every boy like to find his presents on Christmas morning? ~ AHEAP
A28. What organization will not send greetings to the K. K. K. this year? (Abbr.). ~ KC
A29. What kind of people have nothing on for Christmas? ~ NAKED
A31. What is it that some people try to burn at both ends? ~ TAPER
A32. What type of headgear will Santa wear in Chicago? ~ BASINET
A34. What word means "to soak"? ~ RET
A35. What did Santa say in Cuba when asked if he wanted a nip? ~ SI
A36. What means of transportation will Santa use this year? ~ MOTOR
A37. What are the only things a chorus girl tries to conceal? ~ MOLES
A39. What will the turkey be roasted on? ~ PAN
A40. What is the native name for Persia? ~ IRAN
A41. Who hangs the mistletoe? ~ CUPID
A42. What do murderers do when they reach the end of their rope? ~ HANG
A43. What makes the snow disappear? ~ SOL
A44. What lurks in Santa's path when he travels through Chicago? ~ PERIL
A45. What word means species; classifies? ~ SORTS
A46. What is an abbreviation for "Ten Nights"? ~ TN
A47. How will the eook appear the day after Christmas? ~ WAN
A48. What is usually rendered by the choir on Christmas eve? ~ CANTATA
A50. What has its ups and downs in the fashion world? ~ WAIST
A52. What word means lug; tote; fetch? ~ CARRY
A54. Name an exclamation denoting inquiry. ~ EH
A56. Name something it never does in 69 horizontal. ~ SNOWS
A58. Name something that blossoms forth at a coming-out party. ~ BUD
A59. Where does an I. C. S. graduate receive his diploma? (Abbr.). ~ PO
A60. What usually drains the keg? ~ TAP
A62. What word means to "warble"? ~ TRILL
A64. What, in chemistry, is salt? ~ SAL
A65. What word means "verbal"? ~ ORAL
A67. What mollusk does the small boy think Santa travels on? ~ SNAIL
A69. In what region will Santa have no trouble locating the fire-place? ~ HELL
A70. What is the sulphate of magnesia? ~ EPSOM
A71. From what will many people get the Christmas spirit? ~ SPEAKEASY

D1. What is the wisest thing to do when struggling toward the top? ~ CLIMB
D2. Where do college boys eat during the Holidays? ~ HOME
D3. Name something that opportunity never repeats. ~ RAP
D4. Where does a groundhog stay during the winter? ~ IN
D5. Name a preposition denoting destination. ~ TO
D6. What should Santa leave at the old maid's home? ~ MAN
D7. Name a place where Santa wears a kimono. ~ ASIA
D8. Name something worth seeing. ~ SIGHT
D10. What is the third person singular of the verb "to be"? ~ IS
D11. Name a difficult thing for a Londoner to see through. ~ FOG
D12. What word means copped; purloined; snitched? ~ TOOK
D13. What do women put up for the winter? (Apol. to Holmgren) ~ STOCKINGS
D16. What do the people get at barber shops and nightclubs? ~ SHEARED
D19. What is a Mohammedan mendicant priest? ~ FAKIR
D21. What makes the employees of the Government see red? ~ TAPES
D24. What do you call a member of an ancient order of stone-cutters? ~ MASON
D25. In what did Daniel become a charter member of the Lion Tamers? ~ DEN
D27. What is the goat of the Navy? ~ PET
D29. What word means "pertaining to birth"? ~ NATAL
D30. What is an objection or exception? ~ DEMUR
D32. What non-metallic element occurs abundantly in borax? ~ BORON
D33. What is a good subject for an argument? ~ TOPIC
D35. Who gives cheerfully at father's expense? ~ SANTA
D36. What incites promiscuous kissing? ~ MISTLETOE
D38. Name an ornamental shrub with pale purple flowers. ~ LILAC
D39. Name something that is always gay where the host has read "Here's How." ~ PARTY
D41. What do you call the critics of American liberty? ~ CENSORS
D42. Name a miserly thing to do. ~ HOARD
D44. Name something very colorful. ~ PAINT
D45. How do flappers walk before the eyes of man? ~ STRUT
D47. What is the past tense of the verb "to be"? ~ WAS
D49. How do dry agents get their men? ~ NAB
D51. Name something that always comes in pairs. ~ TWINS
D53. What hangs around every Christmas? ~ HOLLY
D55. What produces heavenly music? ~ HARP
D57. What does a too ardent lover often receive for his trouble? ~ SLAP
D59. What were Huck Finn and Tom Sawyer? ~ PALS
D61. What is a step in Paris? ~ PAS
D63. Name something that never rings true. ~ LIE
D64. Name something that will never go dry. ~ SEA
D66. What word means "behold"? ~ LO
D68. Name a note in the musical scale. ~ LA
D69. What is the male personified? ~ HE


Misprints, kept as printed (printed → meant):
A47: How will the eook appear the day after Christmas? → cook

